## Tech Stack

- Framework: Next.js 16 (App Router) with React 19.2
- Language: TypeScript 5
- Styling: Tailwind CSS v4 with shadcn/ui components
- Auth: Supabase Auth (client at lib/supabase/client.ts, server at lib/supabase/server.ts)
- Database: Neon PostgreSQL (primary data store for signals, profiles, orgs)
- AI: Vercel AI SDK v6 (ai@6.0.6)
- File parsing: xlsx for Excel/CSV
- Hosting: Vercel
- Icons: lucide-react (^0.454.0)
- Forms: react-hook-form + zod
- Charts: Recharts via shadcn/ui chart components
- Date utils: date-fns 4.1.0


## Architecture

### Route Groups
- `app/(protected)/*` - Customer-facing pages (auth-guarded, mobile-first, bottom nav)
- `app/admin/*` - Admin panel (sidebar nav, desktop layout)
- `app/auth/*` - Authentication flows (login, signup, onboarding)
- `app/api/*` - API routes (REST endpoints)

### Database (Dual: Supabase Auth + Neon Data)
- Supabase: Used ONLY for authentication (auth.users, session management)
- Neon: Used for ALL application data (signals, profiles, orgs, uploads, data points)
- Connection: `import { neon } from "@neondatabase/serverless"` then `const sql = neon(process.env.NEON_DATABASE_URL!)`
- The `profiles` table in Neon is linked to Supabase auth.users via `profiles.id = auth.user.id`

### Supabase Clients (Auth Only)
- `lib/supabase/client.ts` - Browser/client components. Uses `createBrowserClient()`.
- `lib/supabase/server.ts` - Server components and API routes. Uses `createServerClient()` with cookies.
- `lib/supabase/admin.ts` - Service role client for admin operations.

### Key Services (lib/)
- `signals-service.ts` - CRUD for signals table (Neon). Core read path for /signals page.
- `interpretation-service.ts` - AI interpretation (5-section analysis)
- `organization-service.ts` - Organization management
- `admin-service.ts` - Admin user management
- `csv-parser.ts` / `xlsx-parser.ts` - File parsing utilities
- `zoho-api-client.ts` - Zoho CRM/Desk REST API client (needs wiring to generate pipeline)
- `zoho-oauth-service.ts` - Zoho OAuth token management
- `zoho-desk-processor.ts` - Processes Zoho Desk data into rows
- `zoho-signal-discovery.ts` - Zoho-specific signal definitions (needs migration to new pipeline)

### Deprecated Services (still in codebase, NOT used by active flows)
- `signal-discovery-service.ts` - Old AI-powered signal detection with 92 definitions. REPLACED by 3-question upload flow.
- `signal-calculation-service.ts` - Old heuristic calculation. REPLACED by spec-driven calculation in generate route.
- `staging-service.ts` - Old staging pipeline. Not used.
- `intelligent-mapping-service.ts` - Old field mapping. Not used.
- `upload-page-client.tsx` - Old upload component. REPLACED by upload-proto-client.tsx.
- `signal-discovery-panel.tsx` - Old discovery panel. Not used.
- `upload-modal.tsx` - Old upload modal. Not used.


### Critical Pipeline (MSS - Current)

This is the active data flow. Every change to these files needs extra care:

\`\`\`
Upload CSV/XLSX (upload-proto-client.tsx)
  -> User classifies each tab via 3 questions:
     Q1: What does each row represent? (leads/deals/tickets/customers/events/agents)
     Q2: Which column is the main metric? (dropdown of numeric columns, or "just count rows")
     Q3: Which column is the date? (dropdown of date columns)
  -> POST /api/upload/generate (route.ts)
     - Receives classified tabs + raw row data
     - Generates signal definitions from user answers (NOT from fuzzy matching)
     - Calculates values server-side (count, sum, avg, monthly_rate, group_by)
     - Extracts monthly time-series for trends
     - Upserts into signals table + signal_data_points table (Neon)
  -> /signals page reads from signals table via signals-service.ts
  -> signal-accordion-card.tsx renders each signal
\`\`\`

Key design principle: Signals are generated from EXPLICIT user answers, not from heuristic guessing. If a required field can't be resolved, the signal is skipped (never show a wrong number).


## Database (Neon)

### Core Tables
- profiles - User profiles (id links to Supabase auth.users)
- organizations - Customer organizations
- organization_members - User-org membership with roles
- signals - Computed signals (name, category, absolute_value, trend, trend_value, summary, source_metadata, organization_id)
- signal_data_points - Monthly time-series per signal (signal_id, date, value)
- signal_interpretations - Cached AI interpretations
- saved_signals - User bookmarks
- upload_history - Upload tracking
- integrations - OAuth connections (zoho-crm, zoho-desk, hubspot)

### Key Relationships
- signals.organization_id -> organizations.id (signals are scoped to an org)
- signal_data_points.signal_id -> signals.id
- profiles.organization_id -> organizations.id
- The /signals page queries signals WHERE organization_id matches the user's profile.organization_id

### Unique Constraints
- signals: unique on (name, organization_id) - enables upsert on re-upload
- signal_data_points: unique on (signal_id, date) - enables upsert of time-series

### Migration Discipline
1. Write SQL in `/scripts/` with descriptive name
2. Run against dev first
3. Test the app against dev
4. Run the EXACT SAME file against prod
5. Commit the script to git


## Coding Conventions

### General
- Use TypeScript strict mode
- Prefer `const` over `let`
- Use async/await, never raw promises
- Error handling: always try/catch in API routes, return meaningful JSON errors
- No console.log in production code (use console.error for actual errors)

### Components
- Split pages into page.tsx (server) + *-client.tsx (client component)
- Use shadcn/ui components from `@/components/ui/*`
- Import utility: `import { cn } from "@/lib/utils"`
- Icons from lucide-react only
- Mobile-first: design for 375px width, then scale up

### API Routes
- Always validate input
- Always check auth: `const supabase = await createClient()` then `supabase.auth.getUser()`
- For data queries: `const sql = neon(process.env.NEON_DATABASE_URL!)`
- Return consistent JSON: `{ success: boolean, data?: any, error?: string }`
- Use parameterized queries (Neon template literals handle this)

### Styling
- Tailwind CSS v4 with design tokens (bg-background, text-foreground, etc.)
- Never use direct colors (no bg-white, text-black) - use semantic tokens
- Fonts: Geist (sans) and Geist Mono (mono)
- Spacing: use Tailwind scale (p-4, gap-6) not arbitrary values
- Mobile breakpoints: default is mobile, use md: and lg: for larger screens

### Protected Pages Pattern
\`\`\`tsx
// app/(protected)/example/page.tsx (server component, thin wrapper)
import { ExampleClient } from "@/components/example-client"
export default function ExamplePage() {
  return <ExampleClient />
}

// components/example-client.tsx (client component, all logic)
"use client"
export function ExampleClient() {
  // ... component logic
}
\`\`\`


## What NOT To Do

- Do NOT use localStorage for data persistence
- Do NOT add new npm packages without checking if existing ones cover the need
- Do NOT modify Supabase client files without understanding both client/server patterns
- Do NOT run migrations directly on prod - always dev first
- Do NOT build features outside the current sprint scope (check /docs/DELIVERY_PLAN_MVP_GDOC.txt)
- Do NOT add purple/violet colors
- Do NOT use `space-*` Tailwind classes - use `gap-*` instead
- Do NOT create new service files when existing ones cover the domain
- Do NOT use the old signal-discovery-service.ts or signal-calculation-service.ts for new features
- Do NOT use upload-page-client.tsx or upload-modal.tsx - they are deprecated
- Do NOT import from signal-discovery-service.ts in new code


